  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "dwg_decode_LWPOLYLINE",
    "file": "libredwg/src/dwg.spec",
    "description": "In LWPOLYLINE decoding, the R2000+ path unconditionally reads a points vector via FIELD_2DD_VECTOR(points, num_points, 10) without first ensuring enough remaining input bytes/bits for num_points entries. With crafted truncated object data, this macro-driven loop advances and performs a 1-byte read past the end of the fuzz input buffer, causing ASan heap-buffer-overflow in dwg_decode_LWPOLYLINE_private (generated from this spec). The root cause is missing bounds/availability validation before vector decode, not dispatch in decode.c.",
    "conditions": "Fuzzer input is passed directly to dwg_decode via llvmfuzz. The file must parse far enough to reach an object of type DWG_TYPE_LWPOLYLINE in R2000-or-later decode path (IF_FREE_OR_SINCE(R_2000)), with num_points set to a value accepted by existing checks (<=20000) but with insufficient remaining object stream bytes for all 2DD point elements. This mismatch makes FIELD_2DD_VECTOR read beyond the end of the allocated input buffer and crash."
  },
